Wrong,
        In this case the -fl 0 is passed to aboot, not the booted kernel, It
tells aboot to select the first entry in aboot.conf.

A line like "boot dka0 -fi 1/vmlinux.gz -fl "root=/dev/sda2  1"

tells aboot to get the file on partition 1 of the boot disk, the -fl in this
case gets passed to the kernel. and uses sda2 as root and comes up in single
user mode.

The switch for the aboot decision is the -fi

JJ

