The command is "set os_type nt"    without the quotes, the problem with the
command you used, was you had an = sign imbeded.  POWER CYCLE After entering
the command....

why are you using AlphaBios.  Unless your going to dual boot NT or have an
Adaptec SCSI controller, you should use SRM.  Because? it provides the real
pal-code, not the oem-developers kit pal that's in milo. And they are
different.  With AlphaBios (the group is gone) no longer being actively
developed/supported, work on keeping it current is going to get difficult.

JJ

