you cannot use FAT style partitions with SRM, you must use BSD style disk
labels "b" option in fdisk.

Start the first partition on cylinder 2 to leave room at the begining of the
disk for the boot loader(aboot). After the redhat install boot using
boot dka500 -fl 0

(If it is id5 do a show dev to verify)

JJ
