What about doing a text install?

The Multia's graphics card is a strange beast.  I've never done the
graphical install on a Multia (I do network installs and they seem to
be text based even on RH 6.x), but I have noticed that probing it
duing the installation of the X server can be troublesome.

> When X
> starts the low res gray spotty background comes
> up with the ugly X cursor and everything stops
> (the cursor will move in response to the mouse,
> but nothing else happens).

This might not even be an X problem - might be some other problem
with the graphical install.

By the way, to properly set up a Multia's TGA card, you need to take
note of a few things:

* Whatever resulition you want, you MUST select a 256 color (8-bit)
  video mode.
* Select one (and ONLY one) resultion when xconfigurator prompts you
  to select what video modes you want.  The card supports many
  different resolutions, but X will fail to start if it finds more
  than one modeline.  This one tripped me up the first time I tried
  installing Linux on my Multia.

