>That's a good question; I don't think you have any video cards to choose
>from at present.  There may not be anything really good to use the slot
>for.

My sources of information say 32-bit PCI cards can (in theory) be
put in put in 64-bit slots.  Surprisingly, I read in a technical
book about PCI that you can put a 64-bit card in a 32-bit slot.
The signals that control 32-bit vs. 64-bit transfers are on the
32-bit part of the connector, and the protocol specifies that
mix-and-match should work.

I do have successful experience putting a 32-bit card
(Voodoo3-3000) in a 64-bit slot on a UP2000 board.

(... your mileage may vary ...)

