In 1998 in their wisdom.. The firmware Eng.'s in looking for ways to reduce
code in flash, determined that the "set time" command (to set the toy clock
date and time). was not needed in SRM. This was because both VMS and UNIX
prompted for the date to be confirmed before continuing with an Installation
or update. This is something which should be added to the Linux installs.

The workaround for a Linux install,  is after you enter fdisk to format the
disk, Type -
Alt F3 (I think- its one of them) and you will set another session, set the
date/time then ALT F6 (I think) gets the install screen back, continue with
the install.

on the other session you will have to look where sbin is and set the
complete path for the command, the structure of the install cd is a little
diff from normal.

JJ


