A number of alpha motherboards have tah rather mysterious SROM port
wedged between the PCI slots. From the motherboard manual the most
information I have been able to gather is that it is supposed to be used
to monitor the state of the alpha as it is booting up.
As such, I would expect that you can buy either a 3 1/2" or 5 1/4" LCD
panel for the front of case so that you can watch the alpha run through
it's boot sequence. This said, it would appear that you should be able
to write what you like to the SROM port when the OS has been fully
loaded, opening the possibility that you could potentially start writing
out information about the system to the SROM port. eg load av, uptime,
time, etc..

Has anyone explored this or know of any equipment that can be bought for
use withthe SROM port?

Phil
