I have an AS255 (Avanti) that I've installed RH 6.2 on, which I'm
currently booting from SRM/floppy using the latest MILO image from
gatekeeper. Linux is installed on an internal hard disk connected to an
NCR53c8xx controller.

I recently installed a KZPSA PS (SYM 53c720) connected to an external
shelf containing a TZ87 and two 4.3GB drives.  On power-cycling the box,
SRM detected the additional card and the drives.
Booting using MILO, the on-board controller was recognised, but the
KZPSA wasn't. I assumed this was because the driver wasn't built in to
this version of MILO, so I booted my generic kernel and proceeded to
build a new one.

The generic kernel had a module for NCR53c7xx,8xx, but for some reason
it didn't pick up the new card either.  I built a module-less kernel
containing the NCR53c8xx driver, as the docs indicated that this was the
way to go if an 8xx card was present in the system. I then modified my
milo.conf appropriately. On reboot, the on-board was recognised but the
KZPSA wasn't.  Fair enough, I thought. I rebuilt the kernel with only
the "combination" driver built in.  On reboot, only the internal
NCR53c8xx was recognised. I then tried building both drivers as
modules.  With both modules, as warned might happen in the docs, the
kernel failed to find either controller. I have tried multiple
variations on the themes above, have swapped devices in the PCI slots,
have changed the KZPSA for another, and have had no success in getting
both recognised under Linux.
Booting the box from a DU 4.0f install CD provides access to both
controllers and all devices.

Has anyone got both of these controllers to work in the same box?  I
really need to get the external shelf working on this machine, and have
run out of ideas.

Thanks for any help on this,
Regards, Ger.


