Linux kernel does not have preassigned IDs for things like tape or CD.
Devices are scanned on boot.

There are older drives which has distinct problems with reading CD-RWs
(different reflectivity) and especially if there is more than 600 MB of
data on a disk.  And really often cables and terminations ARE the
problem.

