The roms are the same size, only one can be loaded at a time. The main
problem is SRM was never officially released for the XL's  these boxes were
branded NT only.  The reason was to reduce the cost of the box, by not
requiring it to be tested with Unix or VMS. This meant it would not bear the
Engineering cost associated with SRM/Unix/VMS..

While it is similar to standard AlphaServers, these were build by the PC
group in Kanada Canada. Not on the "Alpha Server" systems line's in Salem
NH(now gone)

PWS433-600, XP's DS's ES's are now built in Houston and Ayr Scotland
