This is what I did 20 months ago.  I don't really recommend it.

Disk /dev/sda: 255 heads, 63 sectors, 522 cylinders
Units = cylinders of 16065 * 512 bytes

   Device Boot    Start       End    Blocks   Id  System
/dev/sda1             1         1      8001    4  FAT16 <32M		# milo
/dev/sda2             2       130   1036192+  83  Linux			# /
/dev/sda3           131       151    168682+  82  Linux swap
/dev/sda4           152       522   2980057+  83  Linux			# spare disk space

Now I'd have:

1 cylinder for milo, or 2 MB whichever is larger
500 MB for / (including /var)
1500 MB for /usr
6000 for /home
~250 for swap
the rest unallocated.  Who knows what you might want to use it for?

Why not install RH6.2?  It's been out for a while.  You can get
an image at:

ftp://metalab.unc.edu/pub/Linux/distributions/redhat/redhat-6.2/iso/

or

ftp://rpmfind.net/linux/redhat/redhat-6.2/iso/

If you don't have a fat pipe, let me know.  I have a burner.

Regards,

