OK ,first of all ,you don't rawrite milo.
Just copy linload.exe and milo to fat partition or floppy (fat).
Then look in CD's image dir ,rawrite generic.img and ramdisk.img
When in milo prompt do this : "boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0
load_ramdisk=1"
When root (generic.img) disk in floppy drive ,milo loads vmlinux.gz named
kernel.
Second string is that milo knows wheres root filesystem and then it looks
line end.
That tells to load ramdisk ,after kernel is loaded it prompts for ramdisk
floppy.

And installer starts.




