I've never seen a paging error, but I imagine that it has something
to do with either reading or writing data in swap or a corrupt page
table in kernel memory.  A couple of things I'd try:

Reformat your swap partitions, checking for bad blocks. man mkswap

Get your memory tested.  It is error correcting memory, right?  I
don't think that any alphas have ever supported non-ECC memory.
Even so, you could be having memory errors.  All it takes is for
two bits in one word to go out of whack and you'll get noticed but
probably unreported memory errors.

I don't think AlphaLinux is fragile.  I have a similar box with
the typical hundreds of days of uptime.

Hope this helps,

Tony Hammitt



