Jack Edwards (jackedwa@mediaone.net) wrote:
: I have an Alpha XL366 running Redhat 6.2 with a DEC 21040 Tulip network
: card.  When I installed Linux it recognized the DEC 21040 and installed the
: de4x5 driver, but during the boot process it always give the error 'Delaying
: eth0 initialization'.

Do you have a line like 'alias eth0 de4x5' in your 'modules.conf'?
Any other options?  Is module really inserted (what 'lsmod' has to say)?
If yes, then what 'dmesg' has to say about it?  If not what happens if
you are trying 'modprobe -v de4x5' (or 'modprobe -v tulip' or
'modprobe -v old_tulip')? Is link light on your card on?  Are you
connecting to a hub or directly to some other card?  Is your network
10 MBit or 100 MBit?  Is your card autodecting it properly?  If not, did
you try to force the issue with options?  Did you try to look at archives
if your question was not answered already quite a few times?
Did you check http://www.scyld.com/network/tulip.html and other
information on that site?

  Michal



