I just finished setting up my Alpha XL 366 with RedHat Linux 6.2 and this is
what I
did.

1. Boot the machine once you see the Alpha XL screen press F2 to enter BIOS
setup.
2. Once in setup, select the Utilites option.  Then select OS Selection
Setup.
3. Press F6 to add a new Boot Option
4. Boot Name: Linux (anything you want)
    Boot File: (location of linload.exe)    linload.exe
    OS Path: (location of linload.exe)    \
    OSOptions: boot  (location of boot directory):/boot/vmlinuz-2.2.14-6.0
root:/dev/(location of boot directory)

    Note:
       Boot File - I have a DOS partition with linload and milo on it and
that is what I specify.  There are proply other                 options.
       Boot File and OS Path have two parts
5: Press F10 to save settings.  It may complain about the OS Path
information but, you can ignore it.  This is really related to booting NT.
6. Leave BIOS setup
7. Select OS to Boot (Linux)

Hopefully this helps.  These are the exact steps I followed and it work
fine.

Jack


