Subject: Re: UDB/Multia: IDE support in Linux?
Date: 2000/05/03
Message-ID: <8eofa0$3aa$1@news.ihug.co.nz>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 618575395
References: <8end5b$1mo$1@finch.mathcs.emory.edu>
Organization: The Internet Group Ltd
X-MimeOLE: Produced By Microsoft MimeOLE V5.00.2919.6700
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

yes.

The Multia supports IDE under Linux - that's how mine works.

It's designed to use a standard 2.5" drive. The original Multia's
shipped with smallish drives (<500MB), but I'm using a 2GB
drive without any trouble, and I believe some people have
even bigger drives.

Of course, if you've got the space, you can install a 3.5" drive
using an adapter.

DO NOT install both a 2.5" and a 3.5" at the same time -
you'll run out of power, and your Multia will start switching off
without warning - trust me, I tried it.

If you want to get a 2.5" cable (or a disk for that matter), look
for an Amiga supplier near you, a standard Amiga IDE cable of
about 2"-3" works fine. You might also be able to find a cable
which will take the IDE out of your box so you can install an
external 3.5" drive.

/Ryan


