First, stay with SRM and aboot.  Install your second hard drive.
at your srm console type show dev. both drives should show up. example:dka0,
dka100 plus the CD usually as dka400 or 500.

insure you graphics card is supported by X (a generic s3 is good)

boot the redhat 6.2 CD

boot dka400 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0"

when you get to the install/update selection click the "use fdisk" button in
the upper right of the screen.

next screen select "use sdb" = thats your new drive.

in fdisk select "b" for bsd style labels.  you need a min of 2 partitions, I
use 4
a = 64meg for /boot
b = swap (512meg)
c=  1g for /
d=  4g for /usr

after the install to boot unix

boot dka0
-------------------------------------
to boot linux

boot dka100 -fl 0
   (The install setup aboot.conf so you only need to pass the "0" flag for
aboot to select the first boot entry.)

Instructions much abbreviated... I only mentioned the important stuff I
remembered :^)

JJ

